Fighting over them getting 25% of their remaining 50% then.&nbsp;




Given usually on an indemnity assessment, they would get 80-90% (or 30-40% of the remaining 50%) of their costs, I think purely from a monetary view, this is may be better deal than 50% interim with 50% on assessment - if we were to run the case to the end
 with the costs assessed. The question is whether we think we'll ever get to assessment! I don't think that we will and I think we can keep the assessment off the cards for a while.&nbsp;




I am relaxed either way and don't feel immediately strongly, but my preference would be to stick as I think we could kick out the assessment until end of the PDD Trial which means we (insurers) are only out of pocket for 50% as of now.&nbsp;




CCing Anna in case she disagrees






























